@brittt_88 It’s actually incredibly complex.

But in general, your assessment is off.

The shortage actually started with Trulicity - and it started over a year ago, long before Mounjaro was available.

@elonmusk @teslaownersSV @chicago_glenn @ianmiles @dcherring @nichegamer Great Job Elon!

I have been on Mounjaro for the last 5 weeks, but had to switch to Ozempic due to insurance (or lack of..) reasons.  Started at 288, weighed today at 261.5.   

Bacon is my new snack food! LOL

@DrKarlNadolsky @DrNadolsky 😂😂 

But seriously:
Started Tirzepatide in a pt w/T1 this past month. Thanks for sharing your case.

https://t.co/u3jcTW0ZLT

@MichaelMindrum 
@LillyDiabetes 
ran into a type 1 person who told me she has a little bit of insulin secretion ability still. She had a CGM. 
her doc using mounjaro "off label" 
She told me her A1c was amazing now.

@nikillinit the active work on hormonal weight loss right now is with GLP-1 agonists/GIP/glucagon pathways. 

Mounjaro is the most advanced drug using these pathways and has a persistent 22% weight loss in 70 week trials.

Main problem is its tough on pancreas

Patient describing Tirzepatide experience

"I feel good and somehow "magically" I can stop eating when Im full and don't keep eating, I have much earlier satiety signaling than before i was on the medication. I think this must be how smaller peoples brains work."

@joinsequence

